A||||8||jimmybpei||4.5l v8 caddy install||||1||
Z||000000||jimmybpei||08-22-2001||05:34 PM||||on suggestion from a guy i recently met in regards to installing a 4.5 caddy motor.<P>i am putting this into an originally 4cyl 5 speed. He has tols me taht this will bolt rite in with not too much hassel. as we there is one on ebay for sale that give a brief description on the install but dosnt stat any <BR>problems on the install process. <P>any help on this would be much appreciated.<BR>paln on starting real soon (this weekend)<P>thankx<BR>Jimm B.||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||08-22-2001||05:43 PM||||Hey JimmyB, how are you doing?  Wasn't that guy me?  Boy you really jump right into your projects, don't you. Did you give up on the 2.8 buildup?  Is this going into you awesome yellow Fiero?  I would like to post pics of your car if you don't mind.  These folks would love to see it. Especially your notchback to GT lights with the notchback trunk.<P>The site you need to go to is <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/</A> <P>He is the main guy in doing this.  Rockcrawl who is on the forum has done it too.  I want to get up to see his install soon. <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||08-22-2001||06:03 PM||||Hey Jimm, Welcome aboard! Here's my Cadero site, hopefully you can get some info from it. <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> <BR>I haven't updated for a while, I have lots more info to put on there. I saw the one on Ebay too, the guy is being pretty generous with his 190hp claim. I'd have to check the books to be exact, but the TBI 4.5 is closer to 150 hp. It wasn't until '90 that they made 180hp (4.5) and '91 200hp (4.9) due to sequential injection and bigger ports and valves. edit&gt; '89 4.5 DFI (TBI) 155hp@4200rpm, 240ft.lb.@2800rpm<P> The rumor about the PFI ECM not working outside the Cadillac is just a myth. I know two guys that are running stock Caddy ECMs and stock programming. They are running in closed loop with no error codes. Both are using Getrag 5 speeds. I figured out why mine was not working but it was too late, I had already switched to a Camaro ECM.<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||08-22-2001||07:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B> I figured out why mine was not working but it was too late, I had already switched to a Camaro ECM.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Rock... have you been holding out on us? Did you figure out how to make the SPI work with a stock Cadillac ECM?<P>Inquiring minds want to know,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||08-22-2001||09:04 PM||||so if i came across a 4.9 i won't have to find the 4.5 intake pieces? that was something that was holding me back (amoung other things). if i tried it i want the bigger of the two engines with all the power i can get.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||08-22-2001||10:28 PM||||The 4.5 TBI intake ports and throttle bores are way too small for a 4.9. Sure it will work, but I'm sure it will also reduce performance. If you want to run a carb or TBI on a 4.9, just leave the injectors in place as dummies or pull them out and plug the holes. Much better than a 4.1 or 4.5 intake.<BR>Getting the 4.9 ECM to work is no problem. There are two UART data lines that need to be looped. I didn't connect them and therefore my scanner couldn't communicate. I had no way to see what was going on. I also found out later that I had the MAP sensor connected to the wrong vac port which caused it to run like sh!t. I had been told it wouldn't work anyway, so at that point I just gave up and switched to the *7730 ECM. Meanwhile Lance Mullen was out in Calif putting his 4.9 in his GT40/Fiero. I sent him a circuit to bypass the PassKey system and that's all he needed. The scanner connects and it runs fine with no errors. The only problem with the stock code is that it has a 4500RPM limiter and probably a 115MPH limiter. I'm still waiting for someone to hack the code to fix these things...Terryk where are you!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||72vinman||08-22-2001||10:37 PM||||Hey Jimmy, check out Jay's site.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/jaygrande/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/jaygrande/</A> <BR>He is here on the forum. It has a description of his N* swap. You have to see and hear it to believe it. Very Very Nice. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Stock Black 86GT||||reg||6
